integration.detail:
Ship '/etc/security/limits.d/95-daw-realtime.conf':
  @realtime  -  rtprio   95
  @realtime  -  nice     -19
  @realtime  -  memlock  unlimited
  @audio     -  rtprio   95
  @audio     -  nice     -19
  @audio     -  memlock  unlimited
Deliberately 95 and not 99: leave headroom above the DAW for kernel threads (threaded IRQs default to 50, migration/watchdog run at 99). A userspace thread at 99 can starve the RCU and watchdog threads and hang the box. realtime-setup's own realtime.conf uses rtprio 99 — this file must sort after it (95- prefix beats its default name) or set your own group.

WirePlumber ALSA device policy — '/usr/share/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/99-daw-alsa.conf':
  monitor.alsa.rules = [
    { matches = [ { node.name = "~alsa_(input|output)\\..*" } ]
      actions = { update-props = {
          api.alsa.period-size            = 128
          api.alsa.periods                = 2
          api.alsa.headroom               = 0
          api.alsa.disable-batch          = true
          session.suspend-timeout-seconds = 0
      } } }
  ]
session.suspend-timeout-seconds=0 keeps the card open permanently — stops the relay click and the 300 ms wake gap that eats the first note of a take, at the cost of blocking runtime PM. api.alsa.headroom=0 is only safe on a real interface; on an internal HDA codec you usually need 1024 or you get constant xruns.
